target:    .github/workflows/ci.yml
gate:      composer test:ci-comment-metrics
kind:      introduce-defect
expect:    says "101 entries"; tests/mutations/FLOOR says
rationale: Inserts a stale registry-size claim as a plain sentence, anchored on two lines that carry no number. The previous form REPLACED the live count line -- the one line a floor bump always rewrites -- so it went INVALID on every bump and had to be regenerated each time, which is a mutation that reports nothing while looking like coverage. Pro's C1 was converted to the same insertion form for the same reason.
---
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -160,2 +160,3 @@
         #
+        # The registry holds 101 entries.
         # A gate wired into nothing is the same vacuity as a gate that asserts nothing, so
